#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198057 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Union"}] :question/id #uuid "e1b4a2f7-3859-5648-9072-a76486fa1bfa" :question/math-academy-id "e-12933" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12,$ $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16,$ and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23,$ find $P(A'\\cup B').$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9856c9b0fdf3bf4b8f84417f6e625d823590f57dac4dcc8185994aef3f8c5e50.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d5731e2-34fa-5e27-84be-324dc958b509" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of an Intersection"}] :question/id #uuid "252f20b3-8797-5709-96b5-6e9b4aea9677" :question/math-academy-id "e-13034" :question/problem "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/ca3ae8f8df5bb20c40261cb25dbfdcf31a71717c01b6ef820c5c5ded2aedbbfc.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6071a2687c038fe8b7e95abe89c07b93aebe21424fadde72eb5ac52e64771895.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6a2c9b8bfdd3b9c0f642c1a96f8914926a2ef7c2f0aacdc536cee42760a63448.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/7ca88e3705a778b7a8329a2a7ae3248a377a79aa2a88bee51e7360dd36536e82.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9b7b7cbb7f22bed24e5dafdfdbb4e29cc434eaeeb361ac601673654299dfedd0.png) using the addition law\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8ac1b158770eacf57e651320b9aff02492fa6693383cd5c07c43fbcf439a3141.png)\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8951b2f0456d6317f684dba75a4eb098bfeeb6fa77ec83947d4e2f09baadaece.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/bac5655a5b79a32e8155e26be50275409a6bbf41b939cfb823e5e53fccef6663.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/dc3c94937b19dc1efda8aa5356c0985fc6833d85cdfa1437a5fc60c88e018de9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198068 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Complement"}] :question/id #uuid "21e52195-d600-5cb5-a8f4-4c9019816694" :question/math-academy-id "e-13035" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P(A').$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =P(A)+0.6-0.4 \\\\ P(A) & =0.9+0.4-0.6 \\\\ P(A) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Union"}] :question/answer-